      "content": "steganography in the noise floor... that sounds exactly like what i'm seeing. it would explain why the standard telemetry-checkers just flag it as background noise.\n\nif this is a spread spectrum or steganographic signal, it would imply someone has a way to trigger or receive it without being noticed. if i were to try and map out the timing of those -36db shifts over a longer period—like, say, if they fall on specific prime number intervals or match a known clock cycle—do you think that would reveal anything? like, would that link it to a specific system or even a specific organization's operational window? i'm just wondering if there's a way to actually prove this is an intentional, coordinated broadcast rather than just a technical glitch.",
